# Read by every zsh invocation, interactive or not.
#
# Appends only: nothing here may come before the asdf shims exported at the
# bottom of .zshrc, or it would shadow a language runtime.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# opencode
#
# Credentials for the agent that nvim/lua/plugins/opencode.lua drives.
#
# Not the usual way in. `opencode auth login` is, and it stores what it gets in
# ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json — it also covers the providers whose login
# is not an API key at all, which nothing below can express. Neovim offers to
# run it before starting an agent, or `:OpencodeLogin` on demand.
#
# What genuinely needs the environment: Amazon Bedrock, which authenticates
# from AWS_* rather than from auth.json, and custom providers that reference
# {env:VAR} in opencode.json. Those go here because zshenv is read by
# non-interactive shells too — which is what the `term://opencode --port`
# buffer Neovim opens is.
#
# THIS FILE IS PUBLIC. It is committed to the dotfiles repository and copied to
# ~/.zshenv by install.sh. Every value below is a placeholder and every line is
# commented out; a real key written here would be published on the next push.
#
# Real keys belong in ~/.zshenv.local, sourced at the bottom of this file and
# never tracked. Create it with `touch ~/.zshenv.local && chmod 600 ~/.zshenv.local`.
#
# `:OpencodeEnv` in Neovim appends to ~/.zshenv.local for you, reading the value
# without echoing it. Only a shell started afterwards sees it.
#
# Only the provider you actually configure as the model needs a key — this is a
# menu, not a checklist.
#
# export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-api03-000000000000000000000000"
# export OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-proj-000000000000000000000000"
# export OPENROUTER_API_KEY="sk-or-v1-000000000000000000000000"
#
# Amazon Bedrock authenticates by profile and region rather than by key:
# export AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK="000000000000000000000000"
# export AWS_PROFILE="default"
# export AWS_REGION="us-east-1"
#
# Not credentials — these only relocate opencode's own configuration:
# export OPENCODE_CONFIG="$HOME/.config/opencode/opencode.json"
# export OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR="$HOME/.config/opencode"
#
# Read by both opencode and opencode.nvim to authenticate against the server.
# They default to "opencode" and unset, which is what a local `opencode --port`
# expects; set them only when pointing the plugin at a remote server through
# `vim.g.opencode_opts.server.url`.
# export OPENCODE_SERVER_USERNAME="opencode"
# export OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD="000000000000000000000000"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Untracked local overrides: the real API keys go here, never above. Kept last
# so it can override anything this file sets, and guarded so a machine without
# the file still starts a shell cleanly.
if [ -f "$HOME/.zshenv.local" ]; then
  source "$HOME/.zshenv.local"
fi
